3|0@MMA^1439947436#cu7r44m:mma_boxing_wrestling$:Hardy throws a big right hand before trading left hooks, which loaded up his left hip nicely. Him not sitting down on the punch left him with poor balance to take the punch, but Condit stepping inside Hardy's stance and aiming his hook shorter caused him to land much cleaner. It's not like Condit's body mechanics on his hook are amazing, and he's off balance enough that he still gets knocked to the side by Hardy's forearm even though he wasn't hurt. Hardy threw his hook too long because Condit tricked him by stepping forward at the same time Hardy was stepping back into stance after pulling his lead leg back to defend an oblique kick, plus Condit stepped slightly off to Hardy's right before exchanging. The distance and angle change made Hardy aim poorly while Condit was right on the money. 
